      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first cabins in Cedar Slope were authorized in 1947 when Tulare County approved an 80‑acre tract, known as Tract 119.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cedar_Slope%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Cedar Slope sits at an elevation of 5,584 feet, giving it a Mediterranean‑influenced montane climate with cold, snowy winters and mild, dry summers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cedar_slope_california",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The first resident of Cedar Slope was Nellie Marshall, an artist and seamstress who arrived in 1881.",
